        "author_association": "MEMBER",
        "body": "Follow-up to #63. Removes the static `TREADMILL_TEMPLATES` array from `frontend/src/utils/cardioTemplates.js` — it was still hardcoded template data in git, exactly what we were moving away from.\n\nThe treadmill dropdown now renders **strictly** from `useDataSource().fetchCardioTemplates()`:\n- signed-in users → live API (`GET /api/cardio-templates`, Cosmos)\n- anonymous visitors → SQLite snapshot (`cardio_templates` table)\n\n`cardioTemplates.js` keeps only the pure interval helpers (`getTotalDuration`, `formatIntervalSummary`), which are logic, not data.\n\n## No anonymous gap\nThe `cardio-template` docs are already in Cosmos, and I regenerated the snapshot (via the `snapshot.yaml` workflow) so `snapshot.db` now carries the `cardio_templates` table with both templates. Verified: table present, 2 rows, default `walk-jog-5x-60` jog speeds `[6,6,6,6,6,7]`. So removing the fallback leaves no empty-dropdown window.\n\n## Verification\n`npm run build` ✓, `npm run lint` ✓ (0 errors), no remaining `TREADMILL_TEMPLATES` references.",
